abstract: >-
  A 5-minute live demo: one real bug (a re-creation of the judge-order bug
  fixed in UK AISI inspect_ai PR #4769) goes to six coding agents in parallel,
  and a deterministic zero-token unittest gate decides who fixed it. The gate
  must be red on the broken code first, checks test receipts, flags edited
  tests and runs held-out spec tests. Measured 2026-10-03: from the bug report
  alone 52 of 52 attempts had green visible tests and 3 met the maintainer
  spec; with the full spec, 12 of 12.
